  "notes": "Diff-derived. getValidState.ts at 2.16.0 assigns a=cohort[0], b=cohort[1], ignoring which slot the user actually set; the fix at 10f8cf1b98 makes it a = stA ?? cohort.find(id => id !== stB) and b = stB ?? cohort.find(id => id !== a). The compare route is /trace/<a>...<b>?cohort=..., so slot B can be set from the URL with slot A left empty, which is the issue's 'search in slot B' case without needing the search page at all. Hazard H3 therefore does not apply to this entry. Predicate uses text_present scoped to the FIRST trace header (nth=0, slot A): on the buggy release that header carries trace beta, on the fixed release trace alpha. The two traces are given distinct root span names so the assertion reads a name rather than a hex id, which keeps the failure message legible."
